// The reflected properties of the HTML elements, as the HTML standard's IDL
// declares them: each [interface, property, attribute, IDL
// type, owner tags, rule?]. `*` is every HTML element (HTMLElement and its mixins).
// Types: boolean, long, unsigned long, double, DOMString (USVString too),
// DOMTokenList (set through its value) and enumerated (a DOMString the prose
// limits to known values; the IDL does not mark those). A property that
// reflects an element (commandForElement, popoverTargetElement) holds a
// reference, not markup, and is left out. test/reflected.test.js walks it.
//
// A numeric row's rule, when it has one: its limit (positive: 0 throws;
// positive-with-fallback: 0 writes the default; non-negative: a negative
// throws; clamped: read back within `range`), and its default. Where the IDL
// leaves the rule to the prose (an input's size, a canvas's size), the prose's.

/** @typedef {{ limit?: 'positive' | 'positive-with-fallback' | 'non-negative' | 'clamped', range?: [number, number], default?: number }} Rule */
